    <string name="import_ref_section_look">1. What this PDF looks like</string>
    <string name="import_pdf_a_format_desc">Table-style timetable: the whole page is a Mon–Sun grid, with courses placed directly in the cell for their weekday and period. The text contains “周数 (week count)” and “地点 (location)” fields and many “星期X (weekday X)” markers. A cell usually holds the course name, teacher, teaching weeks (e.g. 1-16周, 7-12周) and classroom; a double-period class spans two adjacent cells.</string>
    <string name="import_pdf_b_format_desc">Paged / list-style timetable: every meeting is a separate text block ordered by time slot, using “时间段 (time slot)” headers, a “(1-2节)” section notation, a “场地 (venue)” field and “===[第 N 页]” page markers, often ending with a print timestamp. The same course may appear several times (one block per weekday); its weekday is determined by the column the block sits in.</string>
    <string name="import_ref_section_mapping">2. Field mapping rules (how the app reads a course)</string>
    <string name="import_ref_mapping_body">· Course name: the main name in the cell/line (e.g. 高等数学A / Calculus A).\n· Teacher: the person name next to the course (e.g. 张三 / Dr. Smith).\n· Location: a room containing building/room keywords (e.g. 教二楼301, Building B203).\n· Weekday: Monday–Sunday = 1–7; written as 周一 / 星期一 / 星期3.\n· Sections: numbered by small periods 1–12; “1-2节” means periods 1 and 2 back-to-back; “5-7节” spans three periods.\n· Weeks: e.g. “1-16周” = weeks 1 to 16; “7-12,5-7(单)” = weeks 7-12 plus odd weeks 5 and 7; odd/even marks are supported.\n· Optional: credits, course type, class group, zone, note.\nEvery field can be corrected one by one in the preview step.</string>
    <string name="import_ref_section_ai">3. Ask an AI to convert it (recommended)</string>
    <string name="import_ref_ai_body">If your timetable screenshot/PDF cannot be parsed directly:\n1. Take a screenshot of the timetable in the export system (or keep the exported PDF);\n2. Also screenshot the “2. Field mapping rules” section above, and send both images to an AI (e.g. Doubao, DeepSeek, Kimi, ChatGPT);\n3. Ask it to follow the mapping rules and output one course per line, tab- or comma-separated (with a header: name,teacher,location,weekday,sections,weeks), or as Format A text;\n4. Paste the result into the text box here, or save it as .csv / .xlsx and import it with the buttons above.</string>
